{"id": "EUVD-2026-86686", "enisaUuid": "347b944c-5758-311c-8a82-a34bc585ebb3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Preserve inner map identity in callback frames\n\nCallback frame constructors initialize map-typed argument registers with\n__mark_reg_known_zero() and then restore map_ptr. This clears map_uid,\nwhich is the only field distinguishing inner maps that share an\ninner_map_meta template.\n\nWhen a timer callback invokes bpf_for_each_map_elem() on a second inner\nmap, both the saved first map and the second map value can reach the nested\ncallback as the same template with map_uid zero. bpf_timer_init() then\naccepts pairing the timer from the second map with the first map.\n\nThe runtime records the first map in the timer without taking a reference.\nFreeing that map does not find the timer stored in the second map, so a\nlater timer callback dereferences the freed map.\n\nCopy map_uid from the same caller register as map_ptr when constructing\nfor-each, timer/workqueue, and task-work callback arguments. The existing\nidentity check can then reject mismatched inner maps while allowing a\ncallback value to be paired with its actual map.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf85e4f94d7feef8b3c4c90dbe2468595a48393b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/166221c52d3ca332f8699a854efca8e2704bb137", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08b534bafdd9de65b6374474a8fe719c90eb3b01", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66ff2eff093d2a0838f39c713eeb590bc0946c2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b90c5d770dad910fb89e6c1b15052a8a1e8db752"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98033", "GHSA-4746-9qhc-mc6f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14dc1518-9903-3de0-9d22-4212674d37bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69c087ba6225b574afb6e505b72cb75242a3d844 <08b534bafdd9de65b6374474a8fe719c90eb3b01"}, {"id": "2b6231f2-f560-32f0-b6d5-a353935f63f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69c087ba6225b574afb6e505b72cb75242a3d844 <66ff2eff093d2a0838f39c713eeb590bc0946c2a"}, {"id": "31c3e59e-7c5b-380e-bf77-674a3a943540", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69c087ba6225b574afb6e505b72cb75242a3d844 <cf85e4f94d7feef8b3c4c90dbe2468595a48393b"}, {"id": "31f7f3fd-170d-3241-b67d-37821aca0611", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "39df29dd-2d12-3be6-ab80-d4bfdcab45d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "471c8f5b-6800-3494-9f96-3ae8a5033e33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69c087ba6225b574afb6e505b72cb75242a3d844 <166221c52d3ca332f8699a854efca8e2704bb137"}, {"id": "700e5776-020b-3552-941c-463f8d83a792", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "717c1e76-76ad-3192-a6c8-8bc7bfa3a5c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "96b44c35-87c0-37f0-9e1a-81b856987835", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "c63d4867-7e0d-3d17-bd93-dc38c234ac71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69c087ba6225b574afb6e505b72cb75242a3d844 <b90c5d770dad910fb89e6c1b15052a8a1e8db752"}, {"id": "d1b9c31c-6b65-3114-be9e-03c795c576f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "f4508db9-8776-34ea-abbb-2e072630a348", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4081890b-3d7a-3989-8496-5f64bdd4d7bb", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}